public class LocalRateLimiter {
    // Thread-safe Guava RateLimiter for Concurrent Request Limiting (Tier 2 in Stripe)
    private static final RateLimiter rateLimiter = RateLimiter.create(100.0); // 100 per sec

    public boolean checkLimit() {
        // tryAcquire prevents thread blocking (returns false instantly if bucket is empty)
        if (rateLimiter.tryAcquire()) {
            return true;
        } else {
            throw new RateLimitExceededException("HTTP 429 Too Many Requests");
        }
    }
}

try-catch fallback mechanics:
1. RedisTimeoutException: If the Redis cluster powering the Rate Limiter fails entirely, the API Gateway must 'Fail Open'. Dropping all payments because the limiter broke is unacceptable. We emit a high-priority alert and temporarily allow all traffic to pass through un-limited.
2. Clock Drift: NTP sync failures between API gateways can cause race conditions if relying on timestamps. Solved by exclusively using Redis Server Time.

public class ConsistentHash<T> {
    // Thread-safe Treemap mimicking the hash ring
    private final ConcurrentSkipListMap<Integer, T> circle = new ConcurrentSkipListMap<>();

    public void addNode(T node, int virtualNodes) {
        for (int i = 0; i < virtualNodes; i++) {
            circle.put(hash(node.toString() + i), node);
        }
    }

    public T getNode(String key) {
        if (circle.isEmpty()) return null;
        int hash = hash(key);
        if (!circle.containsKey(hash)) {
            SortedMap<Integer, T> tailMap = circle.tailMap(hash);
            hash = tailMap.isEmpty() ? circle.firstKey() : tailMap.firstKey();
        }
        return circle.get(hash);
    }
}

